5:{"event":"Create","id":"F5","note":"The project's refusal doctrine and where TET-28 already sits in the roadmap. README Constraints: "Refusals are format-level, never heuristic. 'You did not point at your evidence' is a decidable question. 'This looks wrong' is not, and belongs in the human-owed partition or nowhere." Two partitions, never a single document-level verdict; machine-checked failures are the grammar/subset/abutting/unsettled/cascade/ledger/verdict/out-of-proof/provenance-drift set; human-owed "none of it is settled by a passing check, and none of it fails the run". README Direction already lists, gated on measurement: "More authoring-time refusals, where they are decidable. Requiring a workspace-rooted search behind a CLAIM THAT NAMES A SYMBOL" — i.e. the roadmap phrasing is mention-triggered — while the same section warns that "several proposed refusals have already been built, measured against a real corpus, and rejected on precision". scope.rs records exactly such a rejection for symbol-mention detection: flagging a module::symbol reference whose module never appears in the fact's captured output "would have flagged a legitimate quotation ... while missing both real overreaches"; "Naming a symbol the code you read calls is normal; concluding about what that symbol does is the failure — and those two are not distinguishable by string matching." scope.rs also states the report-vs-refusal discriminator in this project's own words: the note-outside-extent check is "human-owed, never a refusal" because "a note may legitimately name a location as context ... and only a person can tell that from an unsupported inference. Refusing would make the honest case unwritable to catch the dishonest one."","extent":[{"key":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs","label":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 1-130","world_root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","world_state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e