26:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C3","digest":{"sha256":"03b616ced103c01a25ee534daa66bbab8482543e8ab41853716604d1022f8053"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"supports","pass":"2a166dfea0f07434","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-2a166dfea0f07434","extent":["no-match: look_grep|fn grep|search root in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src","proc: ls /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel (exit 0)","proc: ls -R /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src (exit 0)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs (grep: grep)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs lines 100-245","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs lines 1-100"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"note":"The zero-match branch pushes exactly one entry with key = resolve_key(root_path) and marker from world.for_path(root_path) — both derived from the search root — so key-versus-world_root on that single entry is a comparison of two tool-captured strings that decides whether the bounded negative was rooted at the worktree top. The positive-match branch resolves markers from each matched file instead, so the comparison was never extended there. The -H flag is unconditional and its comment attributes both it and the per-observation marker discipline to the TET-5 work.","pin":"sha256:dc8f725bd5429d41d1726fd70e48deb95b270ba815a6d4c4d9891c941c284d3e","timestamp":1786132738}}
28:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C4","digest":{"sha256":"2cb82786efa57511d6410899a0b1bf00e246c2122a782e7e0f3f6a694eef5e55"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"supports","pass":"2a166dfea0f07434","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-2a166dfea0f07434","extent":["no-match: look_grep|fn grep|search root in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src","proc: ls /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel (exit 0)","proc: ls -R /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src (exit 0)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs (grep: grep)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs lines 100-245","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs lines 1-100"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"note":"Today's positive-match capture records nothing derived from the search root, so no refusal about workspace-rootedness can be decided from it — a capture extension must precede the refusal. The proposed search entry (key = resolved search root, marker resolved from that root) mirrors the shape the zero-match branch already records, making the two cases uniform, and both sides of the proposed comparison are captured by look_grep itself: resolve_key canonicalizes, and no surface lets an author type either string.","pin":"sha256:dc8f725bd5429d41d1726fd70e48deb95b270ba815a6d4c4d9891c941c284d3e","timestamp":1786132754}}
