43:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C11","digest":{"sha256":"6ad46549a1e25cc8bff940431e638e81794b597751f4f2305392814c888f77bf"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"supports","pass":"2a166dfea0f07434","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-2a166dfea0f07434","extent":["no-match: look_grep|fn grep|search root in /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src","proc: ls /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel (exit 0)","proc: ls -R /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src (exit 0)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs (grep: grep)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs lines 100-245","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs lines 1-100"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"note":"grep is invoked with the pattern verbatim via -e, so byte-equality of pattern to symbol is exact: a longer pattern embedding S literally matches only lines that contain the longer string, a subset (strict whenever S occurs outside it) of lines containing S — \"pattern contains the symbol\" would therefore accept a search that under-covers S's occurrences. The dialect limit is real and firsthand: this pass observed that the system grep's default BRE treats '|' as a literal, so a non-literal symbol pattern silently means something else. The kind/pattern fields and the git-backed requirement extend capture shapes verified in F3/F4.","pin":"sha256:dc8f725bd5429d41d1726fd70e48deb95b270ba815a6d4c4d9891c941c284d3e","timestamp":1786133071}}
