52:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C2","digest":{"sha256":"e11c19f300303ce742cbca56065355a0385f8a9f07bd8f8267d7e4896ad32dc3"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"supports","pass":"c1fa7b4466097460","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-c1fa7b4466097460","extent":["proc: find /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src -name *.rs (exit 0)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"note":"look_grep's positive-match arm records one entry per matched file — key = the matched file's resolved path, label \"{file} (grep: {pattern})\", marker resolved from the matched file — and no field of any recorded entry carries the search root; the code's own comment says entries are keyed \"not by the search root or the grep command line\", verbatim as the claim quotes it. A repo-wide and a single-file grep naming the same file the same way therefore produce identical entries (key and marker are identical by construction; the label's file spelling is grep's -H echo, identical for the same absolute spelling). And since a symbol an implementer is told to modify exists in the tree, a genuine census grep for it matches at least its definition site, landing in this undecidable positive-match case.","pin":"sha256:a110390d014d43590c94dbfab4f86eba88ecf0a57fa6fb0665e7801e383d8787","timestamp":1786133848}}
55:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C4","digest":{"sha256":"2cb82786efa57511d6410899a0b1bf00e246c2122a782e7e0f3f6a694eef5e55"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"supports","pass":"c1fa7b4466097460","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-c1fa7b4466097460","extent":["proc: find /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src -name *.rs (exit 0)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"note":"The premise is verified in source: today's positive-match capture records no search-root entry, so no refusal about rootedness can be computed from it, and the proposed root-level entry mirrors what the no-match arm already records (key = resolved root, marker from the root), making the two cases uniform. The decidability statement holds: both sides of the proposed comparison would be captured by the same look_grep call — key via fs-canonicalization of the search root, world_root via git resolved from that root's directory.","pin":"sha256:a110390d014d43590c94dbfab4f86eba88ecf0a57fa6fb0665e7801e383d8787","timestamp":1786133871}}
74:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C13","digest":{"sha256":"65ec3111462b505e233c71d322b17f7471910d2db4c01d383a94c7a20844d878"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"qualifies","pass":"c1fa7b4466097460","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-c1fa7b4466097460","extent":["/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs (grep: objective contradictions)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 1-320","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs (grep: NON_COVERAGE)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 1-80"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"note":"The verifiable half holds: each listed component extends a mechanism I read in source (look_grep's recorded entries, the serde-defaulted world_root precedent on ExtentEntry, the claim verb's authoring-refusal shape, the shared CLI/MCP dispatch, the rendered ledger/Facts tables, and check's machine/human-owed/non-coverage structure), and none of the listed components is itself a code-to-graph link, a commit reference, or dependency propagation. What I could not establish is the clause characterizing those three as \"the mechanisms the TET-27 ticket describes as its subject\": the TET-27 ticket is not in this repository, and reading it would leave the code repository this pass is bounded to. The no-design-debt conclusion rests on that unverified characterization.","pin":"sha256:2458561f0b6cf8055d71f7036cf970edb6ed55efaa4e5c08b439804e6e7f1239","timestamp":1786134028}}
76:{"_type":"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1","subject":[{"name":"C15","digest":{"sha256":"118d12c4f016f580d522b8a3e2e5e4ec4eda7388c6b9d4fb916c175e58522a9b"}}],"predicateType":"https://github.com/lonic-software/tetel/captured-fact/v1","predicate":{"verdict":"supports","pass":"c1fa7b4466097460","reported_kind":"run","source":"proc:workspace-c1fa7b4466097460","extent":["proc: find /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src -name *.rs (exit 0)","/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/observe.rs"],"world":[{"root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"note":"The load-bearing capture claim is exact: look_grep records per matched file only the matching lines (matches.join of the post-colon remainders of grep -Hn output), so an argument value on another line of a multi-line call, or arriving through a variable or default, is absent from the census by construction. The distinctness argument holds — this bounds the artifact's content, where the insincere-examination ceiling (scope.rs, verbatim \"capture makes the extent honest, not the interpretation\") bounds the reading of it — and the remedy genuinely differs: reading the callee and call context, not reading the census more sincerely.","pin":"sha256:a110390d014d43590c94dbfab4f86eba88ecf0a57fa6fb0665e7801e383d8787","timestamp":1786134045}}

2:{"event":"Create","id":"C2","prop":"TET-28's \"workspace-rooted\" requirement is NOT decidable from today's capture in the case that matters most. When look_grep finds matches, it records one extent entry per matched file, keyed on that file's resolved path, with label \"<file> (grep: <pattern>)\" — and the search root appears nowhere in what is captured; the code's own comment says the entries are keyed \"not by the search root or the grep command line\". A repo-wide grep and a single-file grep that matched the same file therefore capture byte-identical extents. Every genuine census of a symbol an implementer is told to modify falls in this positive-match case, because the symbol's definition site matches.","from":["F2"],"timestamp":1786130858}
4:{"event":"Create","id":"C4","prop":"The census therefore needs a small capture extension before any refusal can exist: look_grep should record, for every search, one root-level search entry — key = the resolved search root, a label carrying the pattern and the match-file count, marker resolved from the search root — alongside the existing per-file match entries, making the match and no-match cases uniform. \"Workspace-rooted\" then has one decidable definition covering both cases: the search entry's key equals its own world_root, a byte comparison of two strings the same look_grep call captured from the same canonicalized directory. No author-typed input participates on either side.","from":["F2"],"timestamp":1786130872}
10:{"event":"Create","id":"C10","prop":"The rooting predicate — census entry's key byte-equals its own world_root — is satisfiable and fails closed. On this machine and repo the two spellings (fs-canonicalized search root; git rev-parse --show-toplevel) agree byte-for-byte, so an honestly rooted grep satisfies the predicate; and if the two tools ever disagree on spelling, the mismatch refuses an honest census loudly rather than accepting an unrooted one silently, because inequality can only ever deny rooting, never grant it. Two hardenings belong in the implementation: look_grep should itself compare the canonicalized search root against the marker's root at capture time and store the search entry's key in the marker's spelling when they name the same directory, so check stays a pure byte comparison; and the agreement should be pinned by a test, since one probe on one machine shows the common case, not an invariant.","from":["F6","F2"],"timestamp":1786131346}
13:{"event":"Create","id":"C13","prop":"The feature's implementation surface is small and depends on nothing beyond what this memo's facts describe: one additional recorded entry in look_grep, two serde-defaulted structured fields on the extent entry (following world_root's own compatibility precedent), one new append-only record type with an authoring verb, one rendered section beside the existing ledger and Facts tables, one refusal in a shared render dispatch, and one machine check with its human-owed and non-coverage lines. In particular it requires no TET-27 mechanism — no code-to-graph links, no commit references, no dependency propagation — so shipping it first imposes no design debt on that exploration.","from":["F2","F3","F4","F5"],"timestamp":1786131411}
15:{"event":"Revise","id":"C13","prop":"The feature's implementation surface is small and depends on nothing beyond what this memo's facts describe: one additional recorded entry in look_grep, two serde-defaulted structured fields on the extent entry (following world_root's own compatibility precedent), one new append-only record type whose authoring verb refuses uncensused declarations from one dispatch shared by CLI and MCP, one rendered section beside the existing ledger and Facts tables, and one machine check with its human-owed and non-coverage lines. In particular it requires no TET-27 mechanism — no code-to-graph links, no commit references, no dependency propagation — so shipping it first imposes no design debt on that exploration.","from":null,"why":"C9's revision moved the refusal from the render dispatch to the target verb's own shared dispatch; this claim's surface list still named the render dispatch and would have contradicted it.","timestamp":1786131548}
