94:| C12 | The census's blind spots are boundable from what the capture actually does, and belong in check's printed non-coverage: (a) a textual grep cannot see dynamic dispatch, re-exports and aliased imports, or macro-generated and string-assembled identifiers; (b) the traversal is the system grep's — tetel deliberately shells out to it rather than reimplementing a dialect — so platform rules about symlinked directories and the -I binary skip bound what a "repo-wide" search physically visited; (c) rooting says where the search started, not which tree it should have been: whether the censused root is the tree the memo designs against stays with the reader, alongside the existing per-root tree-state report; (d) whether anyone read the census is the insincere-examination ceiling — capture makes the extent honest, not the interpretation; and (e) under-declared targets, by construction. The report mechanism for printing exactly this kind of standing limit already exists as the NON_COVERAGE list. | OWED |
